It includes patterns adapted from gitleaks
----------------------------------------

The patterns of airlock_pii/recognizers/common/secrets.py for AWS access key ids, OpenAI,
Anthropic and Google API keys, GitHub, GitLab and Slack tokens, JSON Web Tokens and private-key
blocks are adapted from the rules of gitleaks (https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks), file
config/gitleaks.toml as of commit 09242ce9c8a60d9b051fc2d166f9e849b88c7ac0 (2025-11-20). So are
the prefixes and the lengths of the made-up secrets that airlock_pii/synthetic.py generates.
What changed: each repetition has an upper bound, the boundaries of a key are those of a run of
its own characters, and the entropy thresholds and allow lists of the rules are not used.

