The optional Russian NER runs software and models of the natasha project
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Nothing of this is inside the package. The extra `ner-ru` installs three packages of the
natasha project (https://github.com/natasha) from PyPI: slovnet 0.6.0, navec 0.10.0 and
razdel 0.5.0. The recognizer airlock_pii/recognizers/common/ner_ru.py runs slovnet's model for
named entities with them, and builds it the way slovnet's and navec's own loaders do.

The two model files are fetched by `python -m airlock_pii models download` and are not part
of the package either: slovnet_ner_news_v1.tar (the NER model) and
navec_news_v1_1B_250K_300d_100q.tar (the embeddings it was trained with). The natasha project
publishes both, in its own storage and inside its `natasha` package on PyPI. Where copies of
the two files are attached to a release of this project, they are those files unchanged, by
the SHA-256 that airlock_pii/data/models.lock gives for each, under the licence below.

slovnet, navec and razdel are distributed under the MIT License, and each of the three carries
the licence file below. The `natasha` package, where the two model files are as well, is
under the MIT License too: its licence file has the same terms under the line
